
The Pyrope is a generated version of CVA6 using:

export CVA6_REPO_DIR=$(pwd)/YOU_SELECT/cva6
export HPDCACHE_DIR=${CVA6_REPO_DIR}/core/cache_subsystem/hpdcache/
export TARGET_CFG=cv64a6_imafdc_sv39_wb

The following files need to be used to replace Verilog contructs from CVA6 that mix loops + assigns + bitfield which is not supported by inou/slang:
        verilog/fpnew_cast_multi.sv
        verilog/fpnew_divsqrt_th_64_multi.sv
        verilog/fpnew_fma.sv
        verilog/fpnew_noncomp.sv
        verilog/fpnew_opgroup_block.sv
        verilog/fpnew_opgroup_multifmt_slice.sv
        verilog/lzc.sv
        verilog/rr_arb_tree.sv

lhd compile --top cva6 --emit-dir pyrope:tmp_cva6 -- --allow-use-before-declare $CVA6_REPO_DIR/core/include/cv64a6_imafdc_sv39_wb_config_pkg.sv -F$CVA6_REPO_DIR/core/Flist.cva6

The last pyrope regeneration used "Date:   Fri Aug 14 10:56:27 2026 +0100" CVA6 checkout

The verilog directory, only has a small section, so not enough to reproduce the full CVA6
